  "question": {
    "text": "A box contains <math><mn>3</mn></math> coins <math><msub><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math> and the probability of getting heads on the coins are <math><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> respectively. If one of the coins is selected at random and tossed for <math><mn>3</mn></math> times and exactly <math><mn>3</mn></math> heads appeared, then the probability that it was coin <math><msub><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math>&nbsp;is",
